## Claude Code Sandbox

- The managed Claude Code sandbox is enabled (`claude_sandbox_enabled`):
  Bash commands run inside Claude Code's OS-level sandbox.
{% if writable_roots | length %}
- Writes are confined to the working directory plus the managed extra
  writable roots ({{ writable_roots | join(', ') }}).
{% else %}
- Writes are confined to the working directory; no extra writable roots are
  configured.
{% endif %}
{% if allowed_hosts | length %}
- Network egress from sandboxed commands is confined to the managed allowed
  hosts ({{ allowed_hosts | join(', ') }}); connections to other hosts prompt
  for approval instead of failing silently. These restrictions apply to Bash
  commands; the WebFetch tool follows permission rules. The list comes from
  `ai_assistants_sandbox_allowed_hosts` in the dev-setup repository.
{% else %}
- Network egress from sandboxed commands is not allowlisted; connections to
  external hosts prompt for approval. These restrictions apply to Bash
  commands; the WebFetch tool follows permission rules.
{% endif %}
- When a command fails because of the sandbox, request approval to run it
  outside the sandbox instead of retrying; `chmod` and `sudo` cannot bypass
  OS-level denials.
{% else %}

