## Codex Sandbox

- Codex executes commands in its native OS-level sandbox (workspace-write
  mode); there is no managed enable/disable, so the sandbox is always active.
{% if writable_roots | length %}
- Writes are restricted to the workspace plus the managed extra writable
  roots ({{ writable_roots | join(', ') }}); `/tmp` and `$TMPDIR` stay
  writable.
{% else %}
- Writes are restricted to the workspace; `/tmp` and `$TMPDIR` stay
  writable.
{% endif %}
- Network access is disabled inside the sandbox unless enabled in the
  sandbox config (it is not).
- When an operation fails because of the sandbox, ask the user to approve
  running it outside the sandbox instead of retrying; `chmod` and `sudo`
  cannot bypass OS-level denials.
- The extra writable roots come from `ai_assistants_sandbox_writable_roots`
  in the dev-setup repository.
{% endif %}
