## nono.sh Sandbox

OpenCode runs inside the `nono.sh` OS-level sandbox (Linux Landlock) under the
managed `opencode` profile. The launch directory is granted read/write, so work
inside the current repository is unaffected.

### Configuration

- Read/write: OpenCode state (`~/.opencode`, `~/.config/opencode`,
  `~/.local/share/opencode`, `~/.local/state/opencode`), `~/.config/hunk`,
  `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hunk-mcp`, and `$TMPDIR`.
- Read-only: the shared skill directories, `~/.gitconfig`, `~/.config/git`,
  `/etc/gitconfig`, `~/.config/dev-setup`,
  `~/.local/state/dev-setup/applied-version`, and `~/.config/gh/config.yml`.
- `$TMPDIR` is a private `/tmp/dev-setup-ai.*` directory; the rest of `/tmp` is
  denied. Write temporary files under `$TMPDIR`, never hardcoded `/tmp` paths,
  and never grant all of `/tmp` to work around it.
- Network access is not restricted by the sandbox.

### Limitations

- Access outside the grants is denied by the kernel: `Permission denied` on a
  file with normal Unix permissions is the sandbox, not a filesystem problem.
  `chmod`, `sudo`, and retries cannot bypass it. Commonly denied: `~/.ssh`,
  `/mnt/c`, and other paths outside the grants, including other repositories
  under `~/repos`.
- Git credentials are unavailable by design: fetching and pushing private
  repositories fail with authentication errors. The gh CLI aborts at
  startup inside the sandbox: its settings file
  (`~/.config/gh/config.yml`) is granted read-only, but its token file
  (`~/.config/gh/hosts.yml`) is not. Commit and branch locally; ask the
  user to run authenticated Git operations, including gh, from an ordinary
  shell.
- When a needed path is denied, report the exact path instead of debugging the
  filesystem. The user can check it with `nono why`, grant one directory for a
  session with `NONO_ALLOW="$HOME/dir" opencode`, or change the managed
  profile in the dev-setup repository. Run diagnostics and grants from an
  ordinary shell: `~/.config/nono` is outside the sandbox grants and
  prompt-based elevation is unavailable on this kernel. Full details:
  `docs/nono-sandbox.md` in the dev-setup repository.
